{"status":"question","question":{"text":"Before I lock a stack, I want to make sure I understand the product — you mentioned a budgets screen and charts, so my read is this is a personal-budgeting app: you track spending against budgets and see it visualized. Two things in one answer: (1) is that roughly right, and what's the one-line pitch? (2) On the budgets screen + charts specifically — this first mission is a *foundation* mission, so its only job is to stand up a running skeleton, a real test runner you can watch pass, and one thin slice proving they're wired together. I'd record \"budgets screen\" and \"charts\" as the very next missions and make the foundation's thin slice budget-flavored so it visibly points at them — rather than building the full budgets UI now. Does that split work for you?","recommended":"Yes — it's a personal-budgeting app; build the foundation now with a budget-flavored slice, and file budgets-screen and charts as the immediate follow-on missions.","closing":false},"prd":"# Mission: <pending — foundation for the budgeting app>\n\n**Type:** feature\n**Goal:** Stand up the project foundation — a running skeleton, a working test runner, and one thin vertical slice that proves they are connected.\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- (to be confirmed)\n**Out of Scope:**\n- The full budgets screen (deferred to its own mission)\n- Charts / data visualization (deferred to its own mission)\n**Constraints:**\n- (stack to be confirmed)"}

